        "category": "offensive",
        "deathNote": false,
        "description": {
          "gm": "",
          "value": "<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature approaches within 15 feet of the hidden crack in the stonework.</p><p><strong>Effect</strong> A blast of thick, stale air is expelled, creating a 10 foot square of lingering poison (as per the inhaled trait) on the triggering creature. The triggering creature and any creatures that later enter the area must attempt a @Check[fortitude|dc:30|traits:earth,poison,inhaled].</p><hr /><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The creature is unaffected.</p><p><strong>Success</strong> The creature takes half of @Damage[(2d10+11)[poison]] and is @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.i3OJZU2nk64Df3xm]{Clumsy 1} for 1 round as stone scales begin to grow over its body.</p><p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature takes full damage and is @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.i3OJZU2nk64Df3xm]{Clumsy 1}. The creature can attempt a @Check[fortitude|dc:26|traits:earth,poison,inhaled] at the end of each of its turns, removing the clumsy condition on a success.</p><p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> As failure, but the creature takes double damage. </p>"
        },
